messages:
olivia: Quick design callout from usability testing: the eval scorecard is aggressively announcing each example as diffs stream in. Screenreader users reported repeated interruptions when theyrexpand items. This is noisy and breaks flow.

design-bot: A11y report: https://redwood.link/a11y-report-2026 found live-region spam and focus movement warnings.

kai: Agree this is bad. Two options: 1) silent updates with a static status count badge users can check, or 2) batched announcements (summary) after a short quiet period.

ram: Implementation note: current code sets aria-live="assertive" on each diff and also calls element.focus() when an error appears. We should stop programmatic focus changes unless user explicitly navigates.

lena: From PM POV, we need a minimal change we can ship fast that reduces noise but preserves discoverability for SR users. Proposal: keep one offscreen announcer node (role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true") and switch to summary messages like "3 new results" after a 500ms debounce.

qa-bot: Add test cases: NVDA Chrome, VoiceOver Safari. Acceptance: no more than one announcement per user action, and announcements are polite. Auto test: simulate rapid diff stream and assert announcer text updates at most once per 700ms window.

chris: Example debounce helper I'd use:
```js
// simple batch announce
let pending = 0;
let timer = null;
function addResult() {
  pending += 1;
  clearTimeout(timer);
  timer = setTimeout(() => {
    const announcer = document.getElementById('sr-summary');
    announcer.textContent = pending === 1 ? '1 new result' : `${pending} new results`;
    pending = 0;
  }, 500);
}
```

olivia: Two UX nits: wording should be "New results" not "Loading" so it's less ambiguous. Also include a visible, non-modal indicator (tiny dot + counter) so sighted keyboard users get parity.

kai: For keyboard users we should add a skip link in the scorecard that jumps to the first diff and clearly labels the running status. Eg: "Skip to new items (3)" when there are batched updates.

ram: I'll open a PR that replaces assertive per-item announcements with a single announcer and debounced summary. I'll avoid focus() calls. ETA: tomorrow morning. Will gate behind ff_sr_batch_announcements.

lena: Ship plan: roll behind flag, smoke test in staging, enable for 10% of hosted traffic, monitor support queue + a11y telemetry for 48h, then ramp. If regressions, rollback flag.

chris: Also logging: emit telemetry event {screenreader_announce: 'summary', count: n} so we can track frequency. That helps measure if 500ms threshold is too long/short.

qa-bot: I'll add automated scenario and manual checklist to the ticket. Include steps to verify keyboard skip-link and visible counter.

olivia: Lovely. I'll update the design notes and microcopy: "New results available (n)" and add a tooltip explaining live updates. Thanks all :raised_hands:
